    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** serving as our primary offensive engine. With a score of 73.66, he draws an advantageous matchup against Martinez, who struggles with a 4.63 xERA; the combination of a favorable platoon split and his spot in the three-hole makes him our most bankable asset. **Kyle Tucker** (61.35) remains a strong play despite being buried in the order, as his base projection allows him to clear the 60-point threshold even against Mahle. While **Jackson Merrill** (54.13) faces a moderate challenge against Gasser, his role as a green-light runner remains critical in our strategy to bolster stolen bases, a category where he remains one of our most efficient producers.\n\nWe have exercised caution with our bench, most notably regarding **Liam Hicks**. He was our closest call, sitting at a 37.21 efficiency score\u2014falling just short of our 40-point \"Below Floor\" cutoff due to a difficult matchup against Fried and a negative platoon adjustment. Conversely, the lower-tier starters like **Drake Baldwin** (43.58) and **Brayan Rocchio** (42.98) barely cleared the hurdle to stay in the lineup, though **Brayan Rocchio** benefits slightly from wind conditions that may carry fly balls. We remain thin in the infield today due to the absence of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who are both off the schedule, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. Managers should monitor **Sam Antonacci** (49.07) and **Miguel Vargas** (42.79) closely; while they benefit from the wind in their matchup against Espino, they face an elite pitcher with a 2.51 xERA, meaning their upside is strictly capped despite the favorable atmospheric conditions.",
